@*
    The admin shell.

    Its stylesheet is separate from the public site's and is never loaded by it: the site's CSS is
    the thing being preserved pixel for pixel, and an admin style that leaked into it would be a
    slow way to break exactly what this port is measured on.
*@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
    <title>@ViewData["Title"] — Site content</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="~/admin/admin.css" asp-append-version="true">
    @if (ViewData["Wide"] is true)
    {
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="~/admin/editor.css" asp-append-version="true">
    }
</head>
<body>
<header class="ad-top">
    <a class="ad-brand" asp-area="Admin" asp-controller="Edit" asp-action="Index">Site content</a>
    @if (User.Identity?.IsAuthenticated == true)
    {
        @*
            One link, on purpose.

            Overview, Content, Page order and Search listing all read and write ContentDocuments,
            PageRegions and PageSeos - tables nothing serves from any more. The site's words come
            from wwwroot/_data/*.json through ContentStore, and have since Task 3. Those screens
            still compile and still work; they simply change nothing anybody can see, which is a
            worse thing to hand someone than a missing screen.

            They come back rebuilt on top of ContentStore: Task 12 the collections, Task 13 the
            search listing, Task 14 the history. Pictures (MediaController) writes real files
            under wwwroot/_media and is honest today, but it has no way in yet either - it joins
            the editor in Task 12 alongside the image picker it belongs to.
        *@
        <nav class="ad-nav">
            <a asp-area="Admin" asp-controller="Edit" asp-action="Index">Edit pages</a>
            <a asp-area="Admin" asp-controller="Collection" asp-action="Index">Content</a>
            <a asp-area="Admin" asp-controller="Media" asp-action="Index">Pictures</a>
            <a asp-area="Admin" asp-controller="Enquiry" asp-action="Index">Enquiries</a>
            <a asp-area="Admin" asp-controller="History" asp-action="Index">History</a>
        </nav>
        <div class="ad-right">
            <a class="ad-view" href="/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View site</a>
            <a asp-area="Admin" asp-controller="Account" asp-action="Password">@User.Identity.Name</a>
            <form asp-area="Admin" asp-controller="Account" asp-action="Logout" method="post">
                @Html.AntiForgeryToken()
                <button type="submit" class="ad-plain">Sign out</button>
            </form>
        </div>
    }
</header>

<main class="ad-main@(ViewData["Wide"] is true ? " is-wide" : "")">
    @if (TempData["Flash"] is string flash)
    {
        <p class="ad-flash">@flash</p>
    }
    @if (TempData["Error"] is string error)
    {
        <p class="ad-flash is-bad">@error</p>
    }
    @RenderBody()
</main>

@await RenderSectionAsync("Scripts", required: false)
</body>
</html>
